window.products.push({"id":585548,"name":"ClassicPix Canvas Print 20x30: Fallingwater, Also Known As The Edgar J. Kaufmann, Sr, Residence","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":63.32,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51BZWyOSE5L._AC_.jpg","description":"Proudly made in the USA, this canvas print measures 20x30 inches and arrives ready to hang. All of our canvas prints are gallery-wrapped, i.e. the canvas image is hand-stretched over a sturdy wood frame and stapled on rear for permanent mounting. The heavy-duty frame is made with 1.5-inch wood cross bars throughout, creating a striking three-dimensional piece of artwork. See sample pictures above for more detail. About this image... Title: Fallingwater, Also Known As The Edgar J. Kaufmann, Sr., Residence, Pennsylvania Title: Fallingwater, Also Known As The Edgar J. Kaufmann, Sr., Residence, Pennsylvania Notes: Fallingwater is a house designed by American architect Frank Lloyd Wright in 1934 in rural southwestern Pennsylvania, 50 miles southeast of Pittsburgh, and is part of the Pittsburgh Metro Area. The house was built partly over a waterfall in Bear Run at Rural Route 1 Notes: Fallingwater is a house designed by American architect Frank Lloyd Wright in 1934 in rural southwestern Pennsylvania, 50 miles southeast of Pittsburgh, and is part of the Pittsburgh Metro Area. The house was built partly over a waterfall in Bear Run at Rural Route 1 Creator: Highsmith, Carol M., 1946-, photographer Creator: Highsmith, Carol M., 1946-, photographer Date: 2007 August 18. Date: 2007 August 18. Subject: America Subject: America Subject: Architecture Subject: Architecture Subject: Edgar Kaufmann Subject: Edgar Kaufmann Subject: Fallingwater Subject: Fallingwater Subject: Frank Lloyd Wright Subject: Frank Lloyd Wright Subject: United States--Pennsylvania Subject: United States--Pennsylvania Collection: Carol M. Highsmith Archive. The collection features photographs of landmark buildings and architectural renovation projects in Washington, D.C., and throughout the United States. Carol M. Highsmith (1946-) is an American photographer, author, and publisher who has photographed in all the states of the United States, as well as the District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico. She photographs the entire American vista--including landscapes, architecture, urban and rural life, and people in their work environments--in all 50 US states as a record of the early 21st Century. Collection: Carol M. Highsmith Archive. The collection features photographs of landmark buildings and architectural renovation projects in Washington, D.C., and throughout the United States. Carol M. Highsmith (1946-) is an American photographer, author, and publisher who has photographed in all the states of the United States, as well as the District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico. She photographs the entire American vista--including landscapes, architecture, urban and rural life, and people in their work environments--in all 50 US states as a record of the early 21st Century.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51BZWyOSE5L._AC_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"ClassicPix","source_asin":"B072WJNW4D","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-585548","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B072WJNW4D","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B072WJNW4D","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
